# This .gitignore file should be placed at the root of your Unity project directory
#
# Get latest from https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Unity.gitignore
#
# Recommended: add any editor/OS/tool-specific ignore rules from the Global/ templates as needed.
# See: https://github.com/github/gitignore/tree/main/Global
#
.utmp/
/[Ll]ibrary/
/[Tt]emp/
/[Oo]bj/
/[Bb]uild/
/[Bb]uilds/
/[Ll]ogs/
/[Uu]ser[Ss]ettings/
*.log

# By default unity supports Blender asset imports, *.blend1 blender files do not need to be commited to version control.
*.blend1
*.blend1.meta

# MemoryCaptures can get excessive in size.
# They also could contain extremely sensitive data
/[Mm]emoryCaptures/

# Recordings can get excessive in size
/[Rr]ecordings/

# Uncomment this line if you wish to ignore the asset store tools plugin
# /[Aa]ssets/AssetStoreTools*

# Autogenerated Jetbrains Rider plugin
/[Aa]ssets/Plugins/Editor/JetBrains*
# Jetbrains Rider personal-layer settings
*.DotSettings.user

# Visual Studio cache directory
.vs/

# Gradle cache directory
.gradle/

# Autogenerated VS/MD/Consulo solution and project files
#
# SCOPED TO THE UNITY PROJECT ON PURPOSE. These patterns come from the standard Unity
# .gitignore, where "*.csproj" means "Unity regenerates Assembly-CSharp.csproj on every
# Editor open, do not track it". Left unscoped at the repository root they also swallow the
# seven HAND-AUTHORED .NET project files this solution is built from.
#
# That is not a hypothetical: the existing .csproj files are only tracked because somebody
# force-added them, and the next person to run `git add <new-project>/` gets a silent skip --
# no warning, no error, a clean-looking commit -- and finds out from a CI restore failure
# reading "The project file was not found", which points at the solution rather than at the
# ignore rule. It cost one red CI run on PR #6 to find.
#
# Scoping the patterns to Ironfront_Reborn/ keeps Unity's generated files ignored and lets
# our own project files be added normally.
ExportedObj/
.consulo/
/Ironfront_Reborn/*.csproj
/Ironfront_Reborn/*.unityproj
/Ironfront_Reborn/*.sln
*.slnx
*.suo
*.tmp
*.user
*.userprefs
*.pidb
*.booproj
*.svd
*.pdb
*.mdb
*.opendb
*.VC.db

# Unity3D generated meta files
*.pidb.meta
*.pdb.meta
*.mdb.meta

# Unity3D generated file on crash reports
sysinfo.txt

# Mono auto generated files
mono_crash.*

# Builds
*.apk
*.aab
*.unitypackage
*.unitypackage.meta
*.app

# Crashlytics generated file
crashlytics-build.properties

# TestRunner generated files
InitTestScene*.unity*

# Addressables default ignores, before user customizations
/ServerData
/[Aa]ssets/StreamingAssets/aa*
/[Aa]ssets/AddressableAssetsData/link.xml*
/[Aa]ssets/Addressables_Temp*
# By default, Addressables content builds will generate addressables_content_state.bin
# files in platform-specific subfolders, for example:
# /Assets/AddressableAssetsData/OSX/addressables_content_state.bin
/[Aa]ssets/AddressableAssetsData/*/*.bin*

# Visual Scripting auto-generated files
/[Aa]ssets/Unity.VisualScripting.Generated/VisualScripting.Flow/UnitOptions.db
/[Aa]ssets/Unity.VisualScripting.Generated/VisualScripting.Flow/UnitOptions.db.meta
/[Aa]ssets/Unity.VisualScripting.Generated/VisualScripting.Core/Property Providers
/[Aa]ssets/Unity.VisualScripting.Generated/VisualScripting.Core/Property Providers.meta

# Auto-generated scenes by play mode tests
/[Aa]ssets/[Ii]nit[Tt]est[Ss]cene*.unity*

# Auto-generated cache in Assets folder
/[Aa]ssets/[Ss]ceneDependencyCache*

# Managed-stripping link.xml that BuildPlayer merges out of the installed packages and drops into
# Assets for the duration of a build. Normally removed when the build finishes; a build that dies in
# its postprocess step leaves it behind. Never ours to commit — its contents are whatever packages
# happen to be installed, so committing it would pin preserve="all" for assemblies a later build has
# deliberately excluded.
**/[Aa]ssets/packages-merged-link/
**/[Aa]ssets/packages-merged-link.meta

# Unity writes Assets/_Recovery/<n>.unity when the Editor dies with an unsaved scene, so it can
# offer to restore it on next launch. It is per-machine crash state, not project content -- the one
# observed here held a brand-new empty scene (a camera and a light), was in no build settings, and
# was referenced by nothing. Committing it would put another project's crash in everyone's Assets.
**/[Aa]ssets/_Recovery/
**/[Aa]ssets/_Recovery.meta

# The Unity Performance Testing package writes these two into Assets/Resources when a test run
# starts, so the runner can read the run's metadata back from inside a player build. They describe
# ONE run on ONE machine -- hardware, player settings, a run id -- and the package rewrites them on
# the next run. Assets/Resources is otherwise tracked, so without this they show up as untracked
# noise after every local test run and would eventually be committed by a stray `git add -A`.
**/[Aa]ssets/[Rr]esources/PerformanceTestRunInfo.json
**/[Aa]ssets/[Rr]esources/PerformanceTestRunInfo.json.meta
**/[Aa]ssets/[Rr]esources/PerformanceTestRunSettings.json
**/[Aa]ssets/[Rr]esources/PerformanceTestRunSettings.json.meta

# Scratch output from tools/unity-run.py and the tools/probe-*.cs snippets it runs. The snippets are
# tracked; what they write to the project root is not.
/Ironfront_Reborn/harness-*.txt
/Ironfront_Reborn/harness-*.lock

# This repository keeps the Unity project in a subdirectory.
# Ignore generated Unity folders regardless of project depth.
**/[Ll]ibrary/
**/[Tt]emp/
**/[Oo]bj/
**/[Bb]uild/
**/[Bb]uilds/
**/[Ll]ogs/
**/[Uu]ser[Ss]ettings/
**/[Mm]emoryCaptures/
**/[Rr]ecordings/
**/.vscode/
**/.idea/
**/UnityPackageManager/

# OS-generated files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# Local editor backups
*~
*.bak
/.claude

# Unity-MCP is personal tooling: its config contains a token and its skills are generated.
/Ironfront_Reborn/.claude/
/Ironfront_Reborn/.mcp.json
# TheOneKit writes this per-session module summary to the repo root; it describes the local
# kit install, not the project.
/.t1k-module-summary.txt
# Claude Code resolves project scope against the repo root, so the MCP entry lands here rather
# than beside the Unity project. It holds an absolute path to the local server binary and an
# auth token, both per-machine — each developer registers their own.
/.mcp.json
# Keep the project on the registry package declared in manifest.json. Unity may create this
# embedded copy locally while developing or troubleshooting the package.
/Ironfront_Reborn/Packages/com.ivanmurzak.unity.mcp/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Hand-authored .NET solution (added by the M0 foundation pass)
#
# The Unity block above ignores *.csproj and *.sln because Unity regenerates its
# own on every Editor open. Our backend projects are hand-written source and MUST
# be committed, so they are re-included by name. Add a line here whenever a new
# project joins the solution, or CI will fail with "project not found" on a
# machine that has never seen your working tree.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
!Ironfront.sln
!Ironfront.Net.Protocol/Ironfront.Net.Protocol.csproj
!Ironfront.Net.Protocol.Tests/Ironfront.Net.Protocol.Tests.csproj
!Ironfront.Net.Transport/Ironfront.Net.Transport.csproj
!Ironfront.Net.Replication/Ironfront.Net.Replication.csproj
!Ironfront.MasterServer/Ironfront.MasterServer.csproj
!Ironfront.Tools.LoadTest/Ironfront.Tools.LoadTest.csproj
!tools/SpecChecker/SpecChecker.csproj

# .NET build output. conventions.md section 1.4 forbids committing bin/ and obj/;
# obj/ is already covered by **/[Oo]bj/ above, bin/ was not.
**/[Bb]in/

# Never commit real secrets — .env.example carries the variable names, no values.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Test and tooling output (added with the CI setup)
#
# TestResults/ holds the .trx and coverage.cobertura.xml that `dotnet test` writes
# and that CI uploads as an artifact; artifacts/integration/ holds the per-process
# logs from tools/run-integration.ps1. Both are regenerated on every run and are
# large — they belong in the CI artifact store, not in git history.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
**/TestResults/
/artifacts/
unity-compile.log

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Phase 03 operations output
#
# Certificates carry private keys; the durability CSV, the load-test JSON and the
# local run directory are all regenerated by tools/ on demand. The measurements
# that back a report DO get committed, but under plans/dev-*/reports/data/ where
# they are deliberate evidence rather than incidental output.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/certs/
*.pfx
/loadtest-results/
/.localrun/
durability-chart.html
ironfront.db
ironfront.db-wal
ironfront.db-shm

# Ignore Claude context
CLAUDE.md
unity-editmode-results.xml

# The tools/ python helpers (recount_debt_ledger.py and friends) leave bytecode caches.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Written by the Ironfront/Net/Wire client flow Editor command on every run.
# The wiring it reports lands in Menu.unity, which IS committed; this is the receipt.
Ironfront_Reborn/wire-client-flow.txt
Ironfront_Reborn/build-menu-canvas.txt
Ironfront_Reborn/build-match-hud.txt
tmp/Ravenfield
# tools/playtest-local.ps1 -- the local playtest stack: account database and process logs.
# Consumer state from a hand-run session, never an artifact anyone reads later.
tmp/playtest/

.claude/